WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.735
-Now, Che, I follow you
on Instagram,

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.303
and I love how when you talk
about just things that annoy you

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:05.471
and stuff like that.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:08.741
People get so mad,
but it's so funny to me.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.544
And anyway, just so you know,
I'm a big fan of it,

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.112
and even though I don't
"like" it all the time --

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.914
I don't want to be a stalker.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.851
-Yeah, that's for the best.
-Thank you.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.919
Well, I think, I'd like to play
a new game,

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:22.255
it's called "Go Off."

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.490
-♪ Go off ♪

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.326
♪ Go off ♪

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.994
♪ Go off! ♪

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.829
-All right, here's how it works.
A random topic will appear

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:33.166
on screen, and whatever it is,
you'll have to "go off"

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.101
on that topic for 30 seconds.
Make sense?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.036
-All right.
-All right, here we go.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.704 line:0%
Here's your first topic.

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:43.710 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.912 line:0%
[ Laughs ]
-Oh, man, that's easy.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.880 line:0%
Yogurt with fruit on the side.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.749 line:0%
-That's the first one
to come up.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.517 line:0%
-That's easy, man.
I hate yogurt

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.586 line:0%
with fruit on the side.
You know, it looks --

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.354 line:0%
it reminds me of those --
you know those motorcycles

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.323 line:0%
with the little sidecar?

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.858 line:0%
It sounds good.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.860 line:0%
Nobody wants to be
in the sidecar.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.296 line:0%
Also, you can never get
all of the fruit

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:06.799 line:0%
out of the side
to put in your yogurt,

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.267 line:0%
so they're skimmin' fruit.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.870 line:0%
Put all my fruit at the bottom
so I can have it all mixed up.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.039 line:0%
I like to shake --
I shake the yogurt.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.574 line:0%
I'm a shaker. You can't shake
fruit at the side.

00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:17.076 line:0%
-Oh, my gosh, the sidecar.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.844 line:0%
-It's the second worst thing to
happen to yogurt other than

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:21.714 line:0%
that little sweat -- that little
sweat that comes on the lid.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:22.949 line:0%
You know the sweat on the lid?

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.717 line:0%
-That's a little bonus juice.
-Yeah, the --

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.887 line:0%
Ew!
-Ew. Sorry about that.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.390 line:0%
Let's try another one.
The next topic. Here we go.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.896 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.231 line:0%
"Fake crowd noise
at sports games."

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:42.134 line:0%
-Oh, my -- first of all,
I don't know how there's

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:45.004 line:0%
any sports games right now
in the first place.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.172 line:0%
But the worst part,
don't patronize me

00:01:47.172 --> 00:01:48.741 line:0%
with fake crowd noise.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.344 line:0%
It's bad enough you get
arguments with people

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.045 line:0%
that play sports or that think

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:55.314 line:0%
that they can coach better
than the team.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:57.282 line:0%
And now I got to listen
to fake people?

00:01:57.282 --> 00:01:58.951 line:0%
I don't even know what these
fake people are booing.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.687 line:0%
They could be booing something
important, and now you got --

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:04.890 line:0%
Could you imagine, like, booing
something really important?

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.626 line:0%
You're a real heckler.
You're booing, I don't know,

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:10.796 line:0%
one of...
some bad guy's speech.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:13.132 line:0%
I don't know.
[ Ding ]

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.235 line:0%
That was a hard one,
I'm sorry, Jimmy.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.470 line:0%
-Hey, man, that's whole thing,
man. Go off.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.106 line:0%
-I couldn't think of a bad guy.
-I think --

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.175 line:0%
The crowd noise I would get rid
of, too, but also,

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.877 line:0%
I don't like the cardboard
cutouts of the people.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.812 line:0%
-I hate 'em. It's dumb.
It's like, come on man.

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:29.415 line:0%
-Come on dude. At one of
the things I saw,

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.251 line:0%
there was like a giant dog
in one of the chairs.

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.353 line:0%
-Yeah, we're watchin' sports
because we miss sports

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:35.721 line:0%
and we like sports.

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.590 line:0%
Just let us watch the game.
-We're good.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.992 line:0%
-We don't need to watch
the crowd.

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:41.628 line:0%
-Yeah.
That's not what I'm missing.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.129 line:0%
I'm not missing distractions.
We're good.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:46.565 line:0%
We understand --
I agree with you. Very good.

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.601 line:0%
Here we go, let's do one more,
or a couple more.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.735 line:0%
Here we go.

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:53.806 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.877 line:0%
-Oh, toasters with six --

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.713 line:0%
This is -- first of all,
if you're making

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.549 line:0%
more than four pieces of toast,
nobody wants that much toast.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.385 line:0%
All right?
Nobody -- and if you are,

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:07.487 line:0%
you can wait.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.555 line:0%
You can wait on toast,
right, it's fine.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.058 line:0%
You don't need six spots

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.761 line:0%
unless you're Lenny's
from Lenwich.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.662 line:0%
Do they have Lenwich
all over the country?

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:18.964 line:0%
I don't even know.
-No, I know Lenwich --

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:21.200 line:0%
[ Laughing ]
It's a very New York thing.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.001 line:0%
I thought you were gonna say --
-It's a very New York thing?

00:03:23.001 --> 00:03:25.037 line:0%
-I was gonna say, if you're not
Jim Gaffigan,

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:27.173 line:0%
you shouldn't have
a toaster with six.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.341 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-If you can't get toast right

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:30.843 line:0%
in four tries.
[ Ding ]

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:34.147 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
[ Clapping ]

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.982 line:0%
-I always think that, too.
That was a weird one.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.116 line:0%
Oh, you did it.
That was a great one.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.952 line:0%
Let's do one more.
Here we go. Ready?

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.586 line:0%
Thank you for doing this.
-Let's do it.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:45.424 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:48.227 line:0%
Oh, scuba diving.
-Scuba diving.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.262 line:0%
-I've never -- I can't swim,
right?

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:53.799 line:0%
Spoiler alert.
But I don't like scuba diving

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:56.836 line:0%
because, I don't -- first of
all, I don't like that,

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.838 line:0%
you're really just the ocean's
Bigfoot if you think about it.

00:03:59.838 --> 00:04:02.408 line:0%
Because you walk down,
and the fish don't know

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.009 line:0%
what you are,
and you just in this weird

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:06.379 line:0%
rubber suit with this mask --
You must freak them out.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.114 line:0%
And you're going into their
living room freakin' them out,

00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:10.516 line:0%
you know, you're Bigfoot.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.219 line:0%
You're Bigfoot for the ocean.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.020 line:0%
-Yeah.
-Like when aliens come down,

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.389 line:0%
I don't know if Bigfoot's
an alien,

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.191 line:0%
but when aliens come down
and they're just like

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.592 line:0%
hangin' out and they go back...
[ Ding ]

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.794 line:0%
...that's what we're doing to
the ocean and it sucks.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.228
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:24.497
-That was great. Perfect.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.265
That's all the time we have
for "Go Off."

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.067
You are a good man.
Thank you so much

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.268
for coming back on the show.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:30.969
My thanks to Michael Che.

00:04:30.969 --> 00:04:32.771
We'll be back with more
"Tonight Show."

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:34.140
Hope to see you soon, bud.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.875
-That was fun as hell.
Thank you.

